 "2d82e0306202fa87": [
  {
   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\": [{\"id\": \"T1547.001\", \"name\": \"Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\", \"tactics\": [\"Persistence\", \"Privilege Escalation\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The alert directly indicates modification of HKLM\\\\Software\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Run registry key, which is a classic persistence mechanism using Windows run keys.\"}, {\"id\": \"T1036\", \"name\": \"Masquerading\", \"tactics\": [\"Stealth\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The suspicious svchost.exe entry may represent masquerading by using a legitimate system service name to disguise malicious execution.\"}, {\"id\": \"T1547\", \"name\": \"Boot or Logon Autostart Execution\", \"tactics\": [\"Persistence\", \"Privilege Escalation\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The registry modification targets autostart execution paths to achieve persistence by automatically running code at system boot or logon.\"}], \"identity_signals\": null, \"key_findings\": \"A suspicious modification to the HKLM\\\\Software\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Run registry key was detected on SERVER-DB-02, with a potentially masqueraded svchost.exe entry designed for persistence. This represents a direct attempt to establish boot-time execution of code, which is a hallmark of malware persistence tactics. No identity-based anomalies or authentication irregularities were detected in associated auth logs.\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"severity_rationale\": \"This alert indicates active malware persistence activity on an internal database server (SERVER-DB-02) through registry modification\u2014a classic endpoint compromise indicator. The modification of autostart registry keys combined with masquerading of a system service name demonstrates clear malicious intent to establish persistent execution. This meets the high threshold because it represents activity on an internal host with no evidence that controls stopped the modification, requiring immediate investigation to determine if the payload executed.\", \"confidence\": 0.85, \"recommended_response\": \"Immediately isolate SERVER-DB-02 from the network if the registry modification was not remediated. Perform forensic acquisition of the host to determine if svchost.exe was actually executed, check for additional persistence mechanisms, and review recent process execution logs. Query EDR telemetry for child processes spawned from the registry run key entry. Review access logs for the past 7 days to identify lateral movement attempts. Escalate to incident response for containment and eradication.\", \"rounds_used\": 0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "diagnostics": null,
   "id": "msg_011Ch9xS46EMzAqYTdc7cjyY",
