     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.9, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.75, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a solid triage with well-justified ATT&CK citations and a defensible severity assessment. The investigation correctly identifies the registry modification as a persistence mechanism and appropriately escalates to IR. One minor area for improvement: the identity signals section is empty\u2014while auth logs were checked (good), the analysis would benefit from explicitly documenting what was verified (e.g., 'SYSTEM account modification confirmed as legitimate service behavior' or 'no lateral movement detected in auth logs for the past 24 hours'). Additionally, the analysis assumes the entry points to a suspicious svchost.exe but doesn't clarify whether the path 'C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\svchost.exe' is the legitimate system binary or a masqueraded copy in a non-standard location, which would sharpen the malware assessment. These are minor gaps that don't undermine the overall triage quality.\"}",
     "type": "text"
    }
